# Technion-HebrewManim — Cursor agent hints

## Project rules (authoritative)

Detailed patterns live under **`.cursor/rules/`** (always applied):

| File | Topic |
|------|--------|
| `hebrew-paragraph-wrap.mdc` | `SmartHebWrite`, `Tex`, RTL lines, `assistant.html` Hebrew Lines |
| `manim-graphs.mdc` | `Axes`, plots, points, animation order |
| `manim-voiceover.mdc` | `manim_voiceover`, `VoiceoverScene`, bookmarks, Hebrew Whisper, `--disable_caching` |

## assistant.html (visual builders)

- **Hebrew Lines** — mixed Hebrew + `$...$` math, `SmartHebWrite` / `partition_segments`, optional **voiceover** (bookmarks per segment, intro, Recorder vs gTTS, optional **voice between segments** `b0`, `b1`, …).
- **Graphs & Axes** — interactive axes, functions, points; optional **voiceover** (intro, per-step phrases, optional **between steps**).
- **Positioning** — `next_to` / chain layout on canvas.
- **Animations** — FadeOut, Transform, Move/Shift, Rotate, MoveAlongPath, Scale, SurroundingRectangle; optional **voiceover** (single `s0`, intro + phrase).

Voiceover code uses `transcription_model="base"` and `transcription_kwargs={"language": "he"}` for Hebrew alignment. Prefer **`manim render ... --disable_caching`** when testing voiceover.

## MCP

Server: `manim_assistant/server.py`. Resources include `manim://hebrew-guide`, `manim://graph-guide`, `manim://voiceover-guide` (see README).
